#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184764 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184167 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8976a21e-ecbb-53df-8e11-d4d20d6da57f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A5$, $A4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183194} {:answer/id #uuid "ab224635-a5b8-5a57-9317-72afb534390d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A1$, $A3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183195} {:answer/id #uuid "5f574c40-40d6-5456-8e0b-e769f7d61f00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A1$, $A2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183196} {:answer/id #uuid "78e0656a-186f-550a-995d-bd5a97b8dc47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A4$, $A3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183197} {:answer/id #uuid "7c1f5d2c-d037-552f-a83b-33cad6e0ad28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A3$, $A4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183198}] :answer-field/id #uuid "90535267-04a3-5209-88fc-9a5564318779" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183193}] :question/id #uuid "19147c4b-722c-5ed5-9d91-8a4847b759ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-35626" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[A1] - [A8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n> *If $w$ is a vector such that $x + w = x$ for some $x ∈ V$, then $w = 0$.*\n\n*Proof:*\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x + w|= x & [given] \\\\ (x + w) + (-x)|= x + (-x) & [add- xto both sides] \\\\ (w + x) + (-x)|= x + (-x) & [axiom __] \\\\ w + (x + (-x))|= x + (-x) & [axiom A2] \\\\ w + 0|= 0 & [axiom A4] \\\\ w|= 0 & [axiom __]\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe axioms:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}[A1]: x + y = y + x & [A5]: 1 \\cdot x = x \\\\ [A2]: (x + y) + z = x + (y + z) & [A6]: α(βx) = (αβ)x \\\\ [A3]: x + 0 = x & [A7]: (α + β)x = αx + βx \\\\ [A4]: x + (-x) = 0 & [A8]: α(x + y) = αx + αy\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385324 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184167 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1337dd4f-9280-53a2-a0bf-10fa5a1172ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385326} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b06213-6b70-5fb1-9074-bd29c49e8d32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385327} {:answer/id #uuid "175edfb7-a947-56df-a366-83319bf965d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385328} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4ae0dc-f023-5eac-8d6f-6539fcd8b68a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A5}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385329} {:answer/id #uuid "f383b979-fa8e-5c2b-8977-e24abfd545ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "175edfb7-a947-56df-a366-83319bf965d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385328} :answer-field/id #uuid "6de75fa4-40ed-54ed-9a38-aaf2ba31ee58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c7e8b0d2-1b58-5e69-8702-c53196883e47" :question/math-academy-id "q-35627" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Given any $x\\in V$, if $w$ is a vector such that $x+w=0$, then $w=-x$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
